## Conan generates into the source root - `conan install .` there, and the
## CI workflows configure with `-DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=conan_toolchain.cmake`.
## None of it belongs in the repository: it names one machine's paths and one
## build type, and a committed `<pkg>-config.cmake` wins `find_package` over
## the one conan just generated.
/conan_toolchain.cmake
/conandeps_legacy.cmake
/cmakedeps_macros.cmake
/CMakePresets.json
CMakeUserPresets.json
/conanbuild.sh
/conanrun.sh
/conanbuildenv-*.sh
/conanrunenv-*.sh
/deactivate_conanbuild.sh
/deactivate_conanrun.sh
/*-config.cmake
/*-config-version.cmake
/*Config.cmake
/*ConfigVersion.cmake
/*Targets.cmake
/*-Target-*.cmake
/*-*-data.cmake
/Find*.cmake
/module-*.cmake
# machine-specific Conan cache paths, generated by scripts/gen-vscode-env.py
.vscode/.env

offline/
## SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved
## Apple framework slices and the assembled xcframework
apple/build/
*.xcframework/
## Test inputs and reference output (fetched by cmake/test_data.cmake). The
## bare path too: a checkout that symlinks it to another one must not commit
## the link, whose target is a path on one machine.
/test/data
test/data/input/odr-*/
test/data/reference-output/odr-*/
## PDF CJK CMap input data (fetched by tools/pdf/generate_cid_data.py)
tools/pdf/cmap-resources/
## Adobe Glyph List (fetched by tools/pdf/generate_encoding_data.py)
tools/pdf/glyphlist.txt
## Adobe Core-14 AFM metrics (fetched by tools/pdf/generate_afm_data.py)
tools/pdf/afm/

*.zip
*.svg
*.odt
*.odp
*.ods
*.docx
*.pptx
*.xlsx
*.doc
*.ppt
*.xls
# the bindings ship their own copy of one public test document, since neither a
# SwiftPM checkout, an android build tree nor an npm consumer has test/data/
!apple/tests/Fixtures/*
!jni/testfixtures/resources/**/*
!wasm/testfixtures/*

